    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (81.17) and **Trea Turner** (79.76) leading the charge as our clear-cut elite plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a high xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Yesavage, while **Trea Turner** remains our primary engine for the stolen base category; his matchup against Palmquist, who carries a high 6.00 xERA, is further augmented by a stolen base efficiency factor driven by the pitcher's slow delivery. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (74.33) due to a significant platoon advantage against Lowder, while **Caleb Durbin** (69.13) provides a high-upside play, bolstered by the soft matchup against Freeland and a 90% projected stolen base opportunity.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jacob Gonzalez**, who posted a 42.74, narrowly missing the start over **Chase Meidroth** (48.36). While **Jacob Gonzalez** offers decent underlying metrics, his placement in the 9-hole resulted in a negative order adjustment that proved insurmountable against the optimization floor. Meanwhile, our lineup faces some volatility at the fringes; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (48.55) and **Carson Benge** (46.56) are active despite facing difficult matchups against Manaea and Imanaga, respectively. While both are saved by their leadoff spots and projected wind conditions, their low scores reflect the high risk posed by these elite opposing arms. We will monitor for any late lineup shifts, particularly regarding the status of **Nelson Velazquez** (52.34) as he looks to capitalize on his platoon advantage against Bratt.",
